One quality issue surfaced in review: the first compact decoder stayed under the formal 300-operation cap, but its 252 large modular multiplications leaned too much toward arithmetic stamina. I’m tightening the construction to use reversible add/rotate/XOR color layers. The same theorem-backed reservoir argument remains, while the compact route drops to roughly 80 simple exact operations and the mechanical scan still costs millions.
