+Reservoir vertex `R_j` has a colour modulo a prime `q`. Each shifted-cubing
+layer is a permutation because `q = 2 (mod 3)`. There are `B` copies of every
+colour, and four distinct vertices are an edge exactly when their colours sum
+to zero. Before forbidden vertices are removed, exactly `1/q` of all reservoir
+pairs complete any two-set; afterward at least `eta=1/(2q)` do. The shipping
+presets use `B=2048*m*q^2`, so `r=Bq` is twice the lemma's required
+`32*k*m/eta^3` bound. The generator independently knows a certificate by inverse
+generation: it samples all eight reservoir vertices first and chooses terminal
+colours around them.
 
